  {
    "episode_id": 96041,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/6/96041.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 1,
    "turn_text": "Hello everyone and welcome to the Bulldog Bikes Podcast. This program is produced by the Mississippi State University Alumni Association, and it gives you a look at MSU alumni and friends here on campus and around the world. My name is Sherri Carr Smith, and I'm the immediate past national president of your MSU Alumni Association. With graduation just wrapping up on campus, allow us again to say congratulations to the 3,800 new alumni crossing the stage at Humphrey Coliseum. We are so excited for them and all they've accomplished, and we hope they'll stay very connected to MSU. Before we get to today's interview, let's recap a busy few weeks here at the Alumni Association leading up to graduation. On May 2nd, countless graduating seniors made their way to the Hunter Henry Center for our biannual senior celebration to enjoy food, graduation gifts, and more to celebrate all they've accomplished. This was our first in-person event for spring celebration since 2019, and it was evident by the strong student turnout. We were so excited that we were able to do this in-person this year. The very next day, a great group of new class ring recipients were honored at the Chapel of Memories. This is a very special occasion and in addition, Senator Josh Harkins was recognized as this semester's ring tradition honoree. Harkins is a 1997 MSU alumni and was recently instrumental in establishing a license plate to commemorate MSU's baseball national championship. What an exciting time for our university. Thank you, Senator Harkins, for all your help. Speaking of license plates, MSU license plates are an easy and popular way to show your proud support for MSU. Several states offer the plate, so visit alumni.msstate.edu to check out and find out if your state has one. Now let's hear about today's interview. Michael Guest is an MSU accounting grad who recently spent some time with us on an interview. We are so happy he did and he talked a little bit about his time at MSU and how it prepared him for his career in public service. He is the Congressman representing our third congressional district for Mississippi and we appreciate his time. Enjoy the interview with Congressman Guest. Good morning. I'm so happy to have you join us this morning, Congressman. Thanks for being with us. This is Bulldog Bites. We've been interviewing and talking to people that are Mississippi State alumni and got a great connection with Mississippi State. And we appreciate you taking the time to get with us. I know you're very busy.",
