  {
    "episode_id": 96041,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/6/96041.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 4,
    "turn_text": "Well, I'll tell you, I grew up a Mississippi State fan. Both my parents attended Mississippi State and so from a very young age, you know, we were. I won't say we were mandated to go to Mississippi State, but I think it was somewhat expected. And so my parents, you know, would take me up to Mississippi State games. We grew up listing the Jack Crystal on the radio. And so when I got ready to graduate from high school, from a Brandon High School in 88, it was just a very smooth transition that I was going to end up at Mississippi State. And so both my parents went to school there. I went there. My sister went there. My wife, Haley, who you mentioned, she attended Mississippi State. Her father attended Mississippi State. Her sister. I now have a son who is a junior at Mississippi State. And then I have a senior in high school who will be attending Mississippi State in the fall. We've got just a love for the university on both sides of the family, on both my side, and Haley's side. And Mississippi State is just a special place.",
