    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/6/96041.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 8,
    "turn_text": "For once a master, I was a student association senator. I was probably not as committed as I needed to be the sheriff, just in all honesty. I did enjoy it, but I also had other things that I was doing. And so that was not really something that I was focused on. I was a member of Fraternity up there and had a great experience as a resident officer in the Fraternity. And then also just met some incredible people, you know, from all walks of life. And that's the great thing about when you're in college picked with Mississippi State, the people that you meet from not just in Mississippi, but really all across the South and all across the country. And so made some great friendships, have kept some of those friendships. And just so excited that Kennedy is having that same experience that I had the opportunity and Haley had the opportunity to have. And we're excited that our youngest son Pat will be up there. He actually was up there this weekend. So now he's looking, every opportunity can to get to Mississippi State and he can't wait to start school in the fall.",
