    "turn_text": "You know, 18 years old and you know, you're not really thinking about what's the rest of your life going to look like. And so, but I've taken some accounting forces in high school. And really enjoy those courses. And so my thought was I'm going to start in accounting. And then if I don't like it, I can always transition to some other major, but I really enjoyed accounting. And I thought that that was a good foundational major within the business department over there that you can do a lot of different things with. And so ultimately, after graduating from Mississippi State, I went on to Ole Miss to get my law degree. So I never practiced accounting, but it really helped prepare me for law school and for the things that I would do after that. And so that helped me as I transitioned to law school because I felt like that I had a good grasp on how to study and how to prepare And so, you know, I'll tell you that even though I never use that accounting degree, it has benefited me throughout the entirety of my life.",
