    "turn_text": "Very much so, and quite a number of Mississippians, you know, people who grew up in Mississippi, make people who attended state Ole Miss. Mississippi has a large presence on Capitol Hill. And so we will occasionally have the Mississippians all get together and we'll eat dinner and just kind of spend some time together, kind of reminiscing about growing up in our time in Mississippi. But there are quite a number of people who are from Mississippi who are on Capitol Hill. And that's one thing that we look for as we're looking to hire people, whether that be through the intern program students who want to come up there for the summer, the fall, the spring. And also, we try to make sure when we're hiring full-time employees that if at all possible, we want them to be from Mississippi. We think that is important that we're bringing people to Washington who know this state, who know the district, who know the needs of the district. And that's worked out extremely well, particularly in our intern program. Mississippi State has done a great job of feeding young students into that program. probably the majority of our interns of the last couple years have been Mississippi State students. So between members of the University and then my son who's up there does a good job of recruiting some of his friends to apply for that. That has worked out extremely well.",
